From: GS2107 <gs2107@local>
Subject: [PATCH] econet-eth: RX checksum result, RX ring register fix and idle ring size, fe_regs transfer limit

- RX checksum: frames whose descriptor reports IPv4 or IPv6, L4VLD set and L4F/IP4F clear, from a source port other than the CPU ports, are passed up as CHECKSUM_UNNECESSARY (the vendor eth_rx rule bit for bit, eth.ko 0x11a4..0x11dc and 0x1410..0x1420), under NETIF_F_RXCSUM (ethtool -K eth0 rx off turns it off). On GS2107 (2026-11-14, stag_en on): TCP SYNs with a bad TCP checksum, ICMP echoes with a bad ICMP checksum and two-fragment UDP datagrams with a bad UDP checksum all go unanswered, the last two counted in Icmp/Udp InCsumErrors, and no ICMP frame or IPv4 fragment was among the frames marked. debugfs econet_eth/rx_csum counts marked frames and, among them, those that are not TCP/UDP or are IPv4 fragments.
- RX ring registers: QDMA+0x100 (ring sizes) and +0x104 (low thresholds) hold ring 0 in the low half (vendor qdma_lan.ko); the accessors had the halves swapped, harmless while both rings had 512 entries.
- Idle RX rings (ring 1 of each QDMA, ring 0 of a QDMA without a port) get 32 descriptors instead of 512: 2.8 MiB less on GS2107. With the swapped halves this made the hardware wrap ring 0 at 32 and bulk receive raised RX0 ERR_COHERENT millions of times until the NAPI thread soft-locked; with the fix, pushes, bulk transfers both ways and a multicast/broadcast flood ran clean and nothing reached the idle rings.
- fe_regs: one transfer covers at most 64 bytes. Some offsets in the frame engine window stall the bus when read and hang the SoC (a grep over the whole file did), so cat and grep get -EINVAL; registers are read with dd bs=4.

